<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA to tender for 108,000 tonnes soybeans.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA to tender for 108,000 tonnes soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kaohsiung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association will tender on Tuesday for two 54,000-tonne shipments of U.S., Brazilian or Argentine soybeans, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Traders said the tender, if completed with a purchase, could lure other Taiwan soy buyers into the market -- particularly the unaffiliated and highly competitive Taichung division of the Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association.</p>
<p>The Kaohsiung division comprises Great Wall Enterprise, Ttet Union, President Enterprise and Tai Hwa Oil.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Shipment I	    Tonnes   Date/Location</p>
<p>					U.S. Gulf	  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> U.S.		    54,000   July 26-Aug 9	Aug 10-26</p>
<p>					Argentine/Brazil port</p>
<p>-- or --</p>
<p> Argentine/Brazilian 54,000   July 26-Aug 4</p>
<p> Shipment II	   Tonnes   Date/Location</p>
<p>					U.S. Gulf	  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> U.S.		    54,000   Aug 26-Sept 4	Sept 5-19</p>
<p>-- or --</p>
<p>					Argentine/Brazil port</p>
<p> Argentine/Brazilian 54,000   Aug 21 - Sept 9</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
</text>
